"""aq: a durable task queue for Claude Code agents on the Mac.

Work survives Claude usage limits: tasks wait in ~/.claude/agent-queue/tasks/*.json, a LaunchAgent runner drains
them with headless `claude -p`, sleeps (without calling the API) until the limit resets, then resumes the same
session. Tasks marked fallback=dsh run through dsh (Flash-Next) during an outage; runner=dsh tasks always do.
runner=codex tasks run through `codex exec` (OpenAI Codex CLI, model gpt-5.6-luna). `aq trainwatch` (LaunchAgent
com.taiwong.trainwatch, every 3 min) reads the AI Server 2 train guard's incidents and queues one Codex fixer task when
training stays down (deduped per incident, cooldown, daily cap).

Docs: ~/Documents/AI-Server-Docs/docs/22-agent-queue.md. Stdlib only; light (no compute on the Mac).
"""
